{#
    The sign-in mask — the admin's first real page.

    EVERY VALUE HERE IS ESCAPED BY TWIG, which is the reason this is a template and not a
    concatenated string: `alias` comes straight back from what somebody typed, and `error` is
    assembled from a core response. One forgotten `htmlspecialchars()` in a string version
    would be an injection point that looks like working markup.

    `importmap` IS THE ONE EXCEPTION AND IS SAFE. It is a finished `<script type="importmap">`
    element built by `Importmap::scriptTag()`, which JSON-encodes with `JSON_HEX_TAG` so that
    nothing a project puts in its prefix can close the element early. Escaping it here would
    print the markup instead of applying it.

    IMPORTING TURBO STARTS IT. The vendored ES module calls `start()` at top level, so the bare
    import is the whole wiring — the form below then submits through Turbo instead of a full
    page load. No Stimulus here: the mask has no interactive widget, and loading a second
    library to do nothing is still loading it.
#}<!doctype html>
<html lang="de">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>{{ title }}</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ stylesheet }}">
    {{ importmap|raw }}
    <script type="module">import '@hotwired/turbo';</script>
</head>
<body class="login-page">
<main class="login">
    <h1 class="login__title">{{ title }}</h1>

    {% if error %}
        <p class="login__error" role="alert">{{ error }}</p>
    {% endif %}

    <form class="login__form" method="post" action="{{ action }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="{{ tokenField }}" value="{{ token }}">

        <label class="login__label" for="login-alias">Benutzername</label>
        <input class="login__input"
               id="login-alias"
               type="text"
               name="alias"
               value="{{ alias }}"
               autocomplete="username"
               autocapitalize="none"
               required
               autofocus>

        <label class="login__label" for="login-pass">Passwort</label>
        <input class="login__input"
               id="login-pass"
               type="password"
               name="pass"
               autocomplete="current-password"
               required>

        <button class="login__submit" type="submit">Anmelden</button>
    </form>
</main>
</body>
</html>
